## Why the axiom holds (and what it actually is)

The reason "ask for structure, gate for values" simplifies so much is that it replaces a *materiality* test with a *binding-time* test, and binding time is observable at compile time whereas materiality is a claim about downstream behaviour.

The mechanical basis:

> **A gate is a typed hole. You can only cut a hole in something you have already built.**

So the routing test is:

> Can the compiled prompt be written completely, with this unknown represented as a named blocking hole, such that filling the hole at runtime requires **no edit to any other part of the artifact**?
> - **Yes** → value → gate.
> - **No** — filling it would add, remove, reorder or re-scope a section, workflow step, branch, or rule → structure → ask.

This also collapses your finding 1 properly. Gates and questions aren't two solutions to one problem; they're **one mechanism at two binding times**:

| | Compile-time gate | Runtime gate |
|---|---|---|
| Represents | undetermined topology | unbound parameter |
| Satisfied by | asking (slow) or halting with the named choice (fast) | the operator at run time |
| Failure if unsatisfied | cannot compile | compiles, halts before the dependent determination |

"Ask" is just the interactive form of a compile-time gate. Every section that currently exists to manage the *difference* between asking and gating collapses into that table.

**Two corrections to the axiom before it can be adopted**, or it will misfire:

1. It reads as *all* values → gates. That yields 12-gate artifacts that halt on contact. The full form is four lines: **ask structure; gate material values; default immaterial values with disclosure; invent neither.** Materiality survives — it loses its routing role and keeps only its defaultability role.
2. **Terminology collision.** §3.2 Tier 3 is *named* STRUCTURAL and means formatting, ordering, verbosity, delimiters, output class. Under the new model "structural" means artifact topology — the opposite end of the importance scale. Rename Tier 3 to **presentational** before anything else, and note that **output class is not presentational at all** — it is the single most topological unknown in the file (it decides §6.1 rule 1, §6.3's trigger, gate routing, envelope shape). Its current disposition, "unstated → Class B, override if incorrect," is the worst-placed default in the system.

One retrodictive validation worth registering: **§7's existing Tier-1/Tier-2 split is already exactly the structure/value split.** Tier 1 = source tier ranking, conflict precedence, retrieval-failure behaviour — an ordering, an ordering, and a branch. Tier 2 = as-of date, granularity, sufficiency count, exclusions — four parameters. The file's most carefully reasoned section derived this axiom by hand without naming it. Same for reviewer precedence and residual order, both emphatically Tier 1, both orderings over named entities.

